From fd93d091f1ed45ff35a0fea7bae9813008dea40b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 03:55:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arrange: node-local position-space prototype below (1,1)
 (-DLOCAL11), d-sampled drivers

Prototype for the decomposition study (not for merging): with -DLOCAL11
and LOCAL=1, the subtree of every (1,1) node is searched with bitmasks
over the positions of its two lists (exactly-once and disjoint matrices
built per node, forward checking via label -> position masks). Same
squares on quick.txt and full.txt, but 3.3x slower at N = 7.6k (8x more
nodes without the label-union support filter). LOCAL=2 records the
distinct labels at the (1,1) and (1,2)/(2,1) nodes, time-weighted.
SAMPLE_STRIDE / SAMPLE_OFFSET / SAMPLE_LOG sample r1. The default build
is unchanged (quick.txt 1,770,779 nodes).

research/decomp: dsample.c (diagonal-first search on sampled d),
dsample2.c (two-diagonal-first on sampled pairs), mbench.c (exactly-once
filter vs cached masks + gather).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GSaYLGdzq6d82nBLeSZFgB
